## Knowledge Layer Evaluation

The Knowledge Layer was evaluated by checking the alignment between:
- the entity types and properties defined in the teleontology
- the concepts and requirements expressed in the Competency Questions (CQs)

The core entities (Activity and Location) allow the representation of all user scenarios, while contextual entities such as SkiSlope, HikingTrail, CycleRoute, and ClimbingRoute enable the modeling of domain-specific information.

Overall, the teleontology provides sufficient coverage to address the majority of the defined competency questions.
